{
  "requirement": "The `mdbook` subcommand MUST act as the mdBook preprocessor for HTML books, rendering requirement definitions and linked reference badges. This project's `book.toml` MUST configure `cargo habeas mdbook` as the `habeas` preprocessor, using a repository-local Cargo alias for `cargo run --release -p habeas --`. Consumer books MUST continue to invoke the installed `habeas mdbook` CLI directly.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged the three supplied `{test}` items against the text of `requirements.cli.mdbook`. I did not read implementation source.\n\nThe requirement has four obligations:\n\n1. `habeas mdbook` acts as the mdBook preprocessor for HTML books.\n2. That preprocessor renders requirement definitions and linked reference badges.\n3. This project's `book.toml` configures `cargo habeas mdbook` as the `habeas` preprocessor, through a repository-local Cargo alias for `cargo run --release -p habeas --`.\n4. Consumer books keep invoking the installed `habeas mdbook` directly.\n\n**Obligations 1 and 2.** `tests/repository.rs#fn[mdbook_preprocessor_renders_definitions_between_stdin_and_stdout]` runs the real binary (`CARGO_BIN_EXE_habeas mdbook`).\n- It feeds a serialized `(PreprocessorContext, Book)` pair on stdin. The context uses the `html` renderer.\n- It parses stdout back into a `Book`, so it checks the preprocessor protocol end to end.\n- It asserts that no raw `:::{req}` directive remains, which shows the definitions were rendered.\n- It asserts the shields.io badge URL is present, and it asserts the exact badge-row structure. There are two rows, and each has kind and name badge classes, no `<svg`, and two anchors.\n- For the linked reference badges, it asserts the cite badge text and both link targets: the in-page `#habeas-req-rules.ready` anchor and `requirements-index/rules.ready.html`.\n- It also asserts the generated index chapter, which is consistent with the rendering the requirement describes.\n\n**Obligation 3.** `tests/repository.rs#fn[project_book_uses_the_repository_local_preprocessor_alias]` parses the repository's own `book.toml` and `.cargo/config.toml`.\n- It asserts the preprocessor `command` equals `cargo habeas mdbook`, and that `renderers` is `[\"habeas\"]`.\n- It asserts the alias `habeas` equals `run --release -p habeas --`.\n- Both clauses of the project-configuration obligation are therefore checked with exact values.\n\n**Obligation 4.** `tests/setup.rs#fn[setup_is_repeatable]` runs setup against a consumer fixture and asserts the generated `book.toml` contains `command = \"habeas mdbook\"`. That string would not match a `cargo habeas mdbook` command, so the check separates the two forms. It also asserts the setup is idempotent.\n\n**Other cases.** The text does not require particular behavior for non-HTML renderers. Testing them would be inventing an obligation, so I do not count it as a gap. I found no unacknowledged gaps, and there are no `{fixme}` references.",
